---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About — LicensingMadeSimple" description="A 50-state filing directory: who needs the license and which agency takes it. Cornerstone Licensing files the application.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>About LicensingMadeSimple</h1>
      <p>Who needs the license, and where to file it — for operators in every U.S. state.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container article" style="max-width: 720px;">
      <h2>The problem we're solving</h2>
      <p>Business licensing is confusing by default. Every state has different rules, forms, and agencies. We built this site to answer two questions in plain language: who typically needs the license, and which desk takes the filing.</p>

      <h2>What this site is for</h2>
      <p>This site owns <strong>who needs what</strong> and <strong>where to file</strong>. The <a href="/directory">directory</a> covers collection / ARM, consumer and commercial lending, money transmitters, and mortgage in all 50 states, with adjacent notes on insurance, contractors, and charitable solicitation.</p>
      <p>It does not quote service fees, government fee bands, bond amounts, or processing times. Compare providers and costs on <a href="https://licensestore.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">licensestore.com</a>. Timelines live on <a href="https://fastlicense.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">fastlicense.com</a>.</p>

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>Answer 3 questions in the roadmap wizard to see the license type and the usual filing desk. Open the matching state page for the official agency. If you want the application prepared and submitted, <a href="https://cornerstonelicensing.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cornerstone Licensing</a> does that work.</p>

      <h2>Who handles the filing</h2>
      <p>All licensing work arranged through this site is performed by <a href="https://cornerstonelicensing.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cornerstone Licensing</a>, a U.S. financial-services licensing firm. This site does not reprint their filing counts or approval rates. Read those claims on Cornerstone’s own site.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .article h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin-top: 32px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .article h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .article p { font-size: 0.93rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 14px; }
</style>
